 every public poll by double digits, most recently 54-38 in late September", "D+14 state with a first-term incumbent running for re-election", "All six expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe Democratic; markets price Healey near 96%", "Minogue has narrowed the gap since the primary but remains far behind"], "rationale": "Healey has led every poll by at least 16 points in a state that leans 14 points Democratic, and raters and prediction markets uniformly treat the race as out of reach for Minogue. The latest survey shows Minogue closing from a 24-point deficit to 16, but that still leaves a wide, stable gap.", "watch": "If Minogue's affordability and audit messaging keeps cutting into Healey's standing in upcoming polls, the margin could compress further, though a genuine contest would require a far larger shift.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts governor incumbent Maura Healey, a Democrat, faces Republican Mike Minogue, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. Healey has led every public poll by double digits in a state that favors Democrats by 14 points. Her most recent survey, in late September, showed a 54-38 lead, down from a 24-point spread a month earlier, suggesting Minogue has gained some ground since the primary. Polling averages place her advantage between 16 and 24 points.\n\nAll six expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Healey's chances around 96 percent. Minogue has campaigned on affordability and auditing state government, and both candidates have backed a gas tax holiday, but no poll has shown the race within single digits. The contest remains firmly in Healey's favor heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "ma